 			if (pageIndex >= 0) {
 				text += `#Page ${pageIndex + 1}`;
@@ -727,6 +730,8 @@ export class SupernoteX implements ISupernote {
 			OBJPAGE: '0',
 			...data,
 			text,
+			target,
+			isExternal,
 			bitmapBuffer,
 		};
 	}
diff --git a/tests/input/README.md b/tests/input/README.md
index 8d463bb..6ffb0d7 100644
--- a/tests/input/README.md
+++ b/tests/input/README.md
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@ Add the fixture to `FIXTURE_NOTES` in `scripts/build-fixture-site.ts` at the sam
 
 ## Fixtures
 
+'link-n6-20260016-external-url.note' contains one native external URL link created on a Nomad. Its mixed-case target includes percent escaping, query parameters, and a fragment so URL decoding can be checked without silently normalizing the destination.
+
 'blank-a6x-3.15.27-two-pages.note' contains two pages of handwritten text, and demos the available writing tools. This was done using the blank background template, and contains a link to the first page on the second page.
 'blank-a6x-3.15.27-shapes-rtr.note' conains a single page of shapes, patterns, and handwritten text. Headings and keyword highlighting included in file. This file was created using Real Time Recognition (allows export of handwritten notes as text within the nomad), with the blank background template.
 'test-a5x-20220011-old-pen-ids.note' is the oldest file here — `SN_FILE_VER_20220011`, `APPLY_EQUIPMENT:A5X` — and the only one written with the older pen ids: ink pen `1` (not `16`) and marker `5` (not `11`). Page 1 is two lines of handwriting with a highlighter pass over the first, which is what pins `pen=5` to the marker. It also stores colours as palette *ids* rather than grey levels, and `test-a5x-20220011-old-pen-ids.pdf` — the device's own vector export, committed beside it — is what decodes them: `48` is dark grey (157) and `81` light grey (201), each of the export's colour groups covering one of our decoded groups to within a stroke half width. Reading the ids literally used to cost the page 16 of its 58 strokes, dropped by the ink-presence check as invisible. See the `pen` and `color` sections of `plans/vector-format-spec.md`.
